<mei xmlns="http://www.music-encoding.org/ns/mei" meiversion="5.0"><meiHead xml:lang="en"><fileDesc><titleStmt><title>Rhe 2-478v-b-2</title></titleStmt><pubStmt><identifier>https://corpus-monodicum.de/d/e19f0ade-c7ce-461a-9712-165c4a740900</identifier><respStmt><corpName role="publisher">Corpus Monodicum</corpName></respStmt><address><addrLine>Domerschulstraße 13</addrLine><addrLine>97070 Würzburg</addrLine></address><availability><useRestrict auth.uri="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/">CC BY-NC 4.0</useRestrict></availability><date isodate="2026-11-04"/></pubStmt><seriesStmt><title>Corpus Monodicum</title><respStmt><resp>Edition (Spiele)</resp><persName>Elaine Stratton Hild</persName></respStmt><funder>Akademie der Wissenschaften und der Literatur Mainz</funder></seriesStmt><notesStmt><annot startid="#m-616b5c40-f0ca-445a-8507-c0d668aa7d66" endid="#m-6c6ac076-11e1-4e2d-8c69-8d3ec13cb9e3">q&lt;ui&gt;ui (abbreviation mark with the word written out</annot><annot startid="#m-0e300683-f950-4aa3-a2c0-b8bd03538e8a" endid="#m-ef062a29-6d63-418f-8e14-7f568943ef82" corresp="#m-comment-1"><table><tr><td><ptr target="#m-comment-1-notes-0"/></td><td><rend>]</rend></td><td><rend>Text und Notation geben den Anfang von ((CAO 7484)) wieder, möglicherweise als Anweisung, das gesamte Responsorium zu singen. </rend></td></tr></table></annot><annot type="global-comment"><table><tr><td><rend>The Exhortatio virtutum and the Ordo virtutum include personages and themes that occur earlier in Scivias.

For example,
Scivias Book 2, Vision 7 describes the devil bound. 
In the Exhortatio virtutum, virtues bind the devil in the chants Ligate ergo, O regina nostra, and Gaudete o socii. 
In the Ordo virtutum, the chants O victoria que, O fortissimi, O dulcissima bellatrix, Ligate ergo, O regina nostra, and Gaudete o socii describe the same actions.

Scivias Book 1, Vision 4 presents a lament of a pilgrim soul struggling to resist the devil (Querela anime de via erroris)—the same drama that forms the primary subject of the Exhortatio virtutum and the Ordo virtutum. Both the EV and the OV include a lament of pilgrim souls, Querela animarum in carne positarum. 

Personified virtues (the primary personages in the Exhortatio virtutum and the Ordo virtutum) appear earlier in Scivias in:
Book 1, Vision 2, Section 33
Book 3, Vision 3
Book 3, Vision 4, Section 15
Book 3, Vision 6
Book 3, Vision 8 (with the first seven virtues corresponding to the order they appear in the Ordo virtutum)
Book 3, Vision 9
Book 3, Vision 10
Among these personified virtues, Humility takes a prominent role, as in the Exhortatio virtutum and the Ordo virtutum.
</rend></td></tr></table></annot></notesStmt><sourceDesc><source xml:id="wit-rhe-2"><bibl><identifier type="siglum">Rhe 2</identifier></bibl></source></sourceDesc></fileDesc><encodingDesc><appInfo><application version="0.9.1"><name>Monodi-Zero</name></application></appInfo></encodingDesc><workList><work><identifier>Rhe 2-478v-b-2</identifier><title>Qui sunt hi qui ut nubes*</title><incip><incipText><p>Qui sunt hi qui ut nubes*</p></incipText></incip><contents><contentItem><locus from="478v-b">f. 478v-b, l. 2</locus></contentItem></contents><biblList><bibl>CAO 7484</bibl><bibl type="printed-edition">CM V-3</bibl></biblList><classification><termList><term type="genre">Spiele-Passus</term><term type="genre">Responsorium</term><term type="Editor">Elaine Stratton Hild</term><term type="Endseite">478v-b</term><term type="Referenz_auf_Spiel">Rhe 2-478v-b-2S</term><term type="Endzeile">2</term><term type="SpielName">Ordo virtutum (The Play of the Virtues)</term><term type="Band_Genre">Spiele</term></termList></classification></work></workList><manifestationList><manifestation><identifier type="siglum">Rhe 2</identifier><identifier type="cantus">Rhe 2</identifier><titleStmt><title>Rhe 2</title></titleStmt><creation><geogName role="origin-region">Quellen deutscher Herkunft</geogName><corpName role="origin-institution">Monastery - Rupertsberg</corpName></creation><langUsage><language xml:lang="la"/></langUsage><classification><termList><term type="ordenstradition">Benedictine</term></termList></classification><itemList><item><identifier type="shelfmark">Hs. 2, Riesencodex</identifier><physLoc><repository><geogName role="settlement">Wiesbaden</geogName><corpName>Hochschul- und Landesbibliothek RheinMain</corpName></repository></physLoc></item></itemList></manifestation></manifestationList><revisionDesc><change isodate="2026-11-04"><changeDesc><p>Exported with Monodi-Zero 0.9.1.</p></changeDesc></change></revisionDesc></meiHead><music><body><mdiv type="main"><score><scoreDef><st